  "id": "disenfranchised-grief",
  "term": "disenfranchised grief",
  "definition": "Disenfranchised grief is grief that a person feels but society restricts, minimizes, or does not fully recognize as acceptable to express. It can happen when the loss is not widely acknowledged, such as the death of a patient, student, stillborn baby, or animal companion.",
